<title>USA: Typhoon Winnie approaches China.</title>
<headline>Typhoon Winnie approaches China.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON MASS. 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Winnie is expected to make landfall on the east coast of China between Shanghai and Fuzhou in 18 to 24 hours, independent forecaster Weather Services Corporation said on Monday.</p>
<p>Top winds should be near 75 mph as the storm moves in from the east southeast, but the greatest threat will be from flooding rain over east central China during the next 36 to 48 hours as the storm goes inland.</p>
</text>
